+# Law-reference migration dispositions
+
+Follow-up to #425's P2 review, tracked in #429. This is citation maintenance, not a new
+policy home or merge gate. Global laws remain in claude-config `rules/laws.md` and its
+parity-checked Codex guidance. BLUEPRINT design principles use P1-P12.
+
+## Reviewed active citations
+
+The merge-gate model's references to review rounds (2d), ready publication (2e), aging
+(2f), interacting-base review (2g), and bounded fix attempts (11) cite the global contract.
+Its module documentation and comments now say so explicitly. The ACTIVE plan's review-gate
+reference is likewise global law 2. These qualifiers change neither the model's transition
+function nor its independent specification. This pass checked the canonical law source at
+blob `19a25b32444c9e6a7554fd21cce9859000f3672e`; this record is provenance, not a frozen
+replacement for that source.
+
+## Legacy and pinned material
+
+Unconverted bare citations are not aliases for P1-P12. Determine their source from context
+and provenance. When that binding is unclear, do not infer authority. SPECS documents this
+transition rule. Historical BLUEPRINT-law citations retain the corresponding principle
+identity; dated BOOK and handoff quotations stay unchanged.
+
+The `templates/hooks/dispatch.py` worktree-law comment is in hash-bound floor source.
+Its historical global-worktree binding is retained without editing that file or changing
+its version, canonical digest, extraction manifest or installed copy. Generated/pinned
+comments migrate only with an independently authorized source update, not as collateral
+work in a prose cleanup.
+
+This is the disposition of the named review examples, not certification that every file
+in the estate has been migrated. Remaining ambiguous operational citations stay in #429
+until their own provenance is resolved. No bulk number substitution is authorized.
